What: /sys/bus/spi/devices/.../nav_settings/
Date: October 2026
Description:
        FPC1021 navigation settings recovered from EF67S S0226114.
        Attributes use mode 0660. Reads return "attribute_name: value\n";
        writes accept a decimal integer.

        p_multiplier_x, p_multiplier_y, p_sensitivity_key,
        p_sensitivity_ptr, multiplier_key_accel, multiplier_ptr_accel,
        threshold_key_accel, threshold_ptr_accel, threshold_ptr_start,
        duration_ptr_clear: 0..255.
        nav_finger_up_threshold: 0..12.
        btp_input_mode: 1 (touch), 2 (trackpad), 3 (mouse). Changing mode
        restores that mode's stock defaults. Settings changed during
        navigation restart it; capture uses its own saved settings.

        Input names are fpcMouse, fpcTrackpad and fpcTouchpad. Mouse and
        trackpad report relative movement; touch reports absolute
        coordinates and contact. A stationary mouse contact longer than
        900 ms reports a right click. The stock worker does not generate
        tap/left-click or wheel events despite advertising those
        capabilities; this implementation preserves that behavior.

What: /dev/fpc_btp navigation commands
Date: October 2026
Description:
        Navigation ioctl 0x4004fc04 and legacy commands 5001, 5002, 5003
        take the mode directly in arg (1 touch, 2 trackpad, 3 mouse),
        not a userspace pointer. The legacy command number does not
        select the mode.

        One text write per open accepts the stock prefixes touch,
        trackpad, mouse or stop_navi. A trailing newline is accepted.
        A mode command starts navigation and requests a single restart
        when the file closes. A close during suspend defers that restart
        until resume. stop_navi clears that request.

        Capture and navigation share a serialized sensor worker.
        Capture, cancellation, suspend and removal release any active
        synthetic touch before changing sensor state. Stop/abort ioctls
        stop the current worker but retain an explicit close restart
        request. Suspend retains navigation intent; resume restarts
        only when enabled. An explicit stop_navi remains stopped.
